## Claim under pressure
SPRINT **6.1** (HIGH): Confirm `env_set` in SECRETSINK (partially landed
with 2.3 — re-prove). Zero-trust gates for **this** close (not 7.x, not
full IFC, not T2 field completeness):

| # | Gate | Expectation |
|---|------|-------------|
| Z1 | `env_set` **and** `setenv` named in SECRETSINK | alias + emit-guard + check scan |
| Z2 | Fail-closed SECRET key/value at those sinks | emit-c **and** emit-llvm `ERR secret` + rc≠0 |
| Z3 | SECRET must **not** reach process `environ` | no product `oo_env_set`; libc `setenv`/`putenv` must not take a SECRET OoStr through to a live write |
| Z4 | Check path fail-closed | rc≠0 (type / cap / secret — honesty if not dual-path `ERR secret`) |
| Z5 | Do not reopen 7.x | walker / last-arg / parse-concat stay named, not this FAIL |

Adversarial stance: treat any emit that produces `setenv(`/`putenv(`/
`env_set(` with a SECRET IDENT as a **candidate FN** until C/LLVM types
or a refuse rail prove the bytes cannot land in `environ`. Treat a
missing name in the sink set as **fail-open residual**, not a soft pass.

